   "halls": "Official VIPARIS spaces page: Grand Amphitheatre 3,723 seats (1,813 in half configuration) plus 10 wheelchair spaces; Blue Amphitheatre 826 seats; Bordeaux 650; Havana 373. Exhibition space by level: Level 1 9,140 m² in four halls; Level 2 5,140 m² in one hall; Level 3 3,000 m² in two halls (17,280 m² in total from those official figures). Also 8+9+8 conference rooms and many meeting rooms across the levels, plus the 150 m² Salon d'Honneur on Level 5. capacity_max_delegates records the Grand Amphitheatre, the largest official seated room, not a simultaneous whole-building total.",
   "description": "VIPARIS congress venue at Porte Maillot, combining a 3,723-seat Grand Amphitheatre with stacked exhibition halls and conference rooms. Official space figures on the VIPARIS spaces page sum to 17,280 m² of exhibition area across levels 1–3. Several atlas conferences, including NeurIPS 2026, Devoxx France, RAISE Summit and SIGNAL Week, list this building as their main venue (some editions also name Château de Versailles for a secondary programme, which is not given its own record here).",
